null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927414"}, {"id": "ac7e4d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927415"}, {"id": "c5ff26", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927416"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927417", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb8"], "question": {"text": "If the standard molar enthalpy change for combustion of graphite powder is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the amount of heat generated on combustion of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of graphite powder in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math> (Nearest integer):"}, "options": [{"id": "820c47", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927418"}, {"id": "e86058", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927419"}, {"id": "585601", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892741a"}, {"id": "91d8f4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892741b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892741c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b65"], "question": {"text": "<p>For a certain reaction at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ΔG</mi><mo>°</mo></math> for the same reaction is – ________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math> (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3112f6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892741d"}, {"id": "9da9f0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892741e"}, {"id": "930c11", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892741f"}, {"id": "e080da", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927420"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927421", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["6162fb896ed13040ec850101"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> coal is burnt in a bomb calorimeter in excess of oxygen at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> pressure.</p><p>The temperature of the calorimeter rises from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The enthalpy change during the combustion of coal is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is_____(Given : Heat capacity of bomb calorimeter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>kJK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Assume coal to be pure carbon)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "18877a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927422"}, {"id": "475706", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927423"}, {"id": "e93969", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927424"}, {"id": "df15eb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927425"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927426", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6176f3ee6581241c7072a758"], "question": {"text": "The enthalpy change for the conversion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;(g) to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (Nearest integer)<br />Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mtext>dis&#160;</mtext></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>eg</mi></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mrow><mi>Cl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>350</mn><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>hyd</mi></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msubsup><mi>Cl</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>380</mn><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "99d214", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927427"}, {"id": "ea067b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927428"}, {"id": "a095d9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927429"}, {"id": "8d1f05", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892742a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892742b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b61"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8652;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, ozone is fifty percent dissociated. The standard free energy change at this temperature and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mo>-</mo></mfenced><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Nearest integer)</p><p>[Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "cc0950", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892742c"}, {"id": "898683", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892742d"}, {"id": "ca64fd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892742e"}, {"id": "9494d1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892742f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927430", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6162fb8c6ed13040ec8502c6"], "question": {"text": "<p>When&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> solution is mixed with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>MNaOH</mi></math> solution, the increase in temperature of the final solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8212;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. (Round off to the nearest integer).</p><p>[Use :<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>:</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mrow><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>57</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Specific heat of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;, density of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Assume no change in volume of solution on mixing.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4ae353", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927431"}, {"id": "f9dab7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927432"}, {"id": "6fba3b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927433"}, {"id": "104367", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927434"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927435", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f1a"], "question": {"text": "\\(\\Delta_{\\text {vap }} \\mathrm{H}^{\\ominus}\\) for water is \\(+40.79 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\) at 1 bar and \\(100{ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\). Change in internal energy for this vapourisation under same condition is \\(\\qquad\\) \\(\\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\). (Integer answer) (Given \\(\\mathrm{R}=8.3 \\mathrm{JK}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\))"}, "options": [{"id": "08d354", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927436"}, {"id": "2d6472", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927437"}, {"id": "bbdd21", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927438"}, {"id": "8589dd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927439"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892743a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b65"], "question": {"text": "<p>The gas phase reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8652;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>The equilibrium constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub></math> for this reaction is ___&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Round off to the Nearest integer)</p><p>Use : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bar</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;antilog <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>501</mn></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d9299e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892743b"}, {"id": "dc02f6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892743c"}, {"id": "479194", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892743d"}, {"id": "c1c6f4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892743e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892743f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6228bb8f5339ae4f88133302"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8652;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>For the given reaction, if the initial pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>450</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mmHg</mi></math> and the pressure at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>720</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mmHg</mi></math> at a constant temperature<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and constant volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The fraction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decomposed under these conditions is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (nearest integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3edae5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927440"}, {"id": "d81625", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927441"}, {"id": "e6acc1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927442"}, {"id": "a7e751", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927443"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927444", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8fd4"], "question": {"text": "<p>The magnitude of work done by a gas that undergoes a reversible expansion along the path <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> shown in the figure is _________.<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9136f031-6ceb-47d9-9b2d-8ab09eb1dbd9-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 506px; height: 345px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "da56ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927445"}, {"id": "4a43b6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927446"}, {"id": "2e79c6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927447"}, {"id": "4dbf43", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927448"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927449", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b61"], "question": {"text": "<p>The incorrect statements from the following is:<br />A.&nbsp;The electrical work that a reaction can perform at constant pressure and temperature is equal to the reaction Gibbs energy.<br />B.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi>cell</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp; is dependent on the pressure.<br />C.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>dE</mi><mi>cell</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></msubsup><mi>dT</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></mrow><mi>nF</mi></mfrac></math><br />D. A cell is operating reversibly if the cell potential is exactly balanced by an opposing source of potential difference.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6628e1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892744a"}, {"id": "d8e312", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892744b"}, {"id": "71eddf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892744c"}, {"id": "476781", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892744d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892744e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["61adb568dec0c790740ac549"], "question": {"text": "A gas ( Molar mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>280</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) was burnt in excess <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in a constant volume calorimeter and during combustion the temperature of calorimeter increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. If the heat capacity of calorimeter is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and enthalpy of combustion of gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> then amount of gas burnt is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "83ba22", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a892744f"}, {"id": "3534d1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927450"}, {"id": "e20d5e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927451"}, {"id": "3c11e9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927452"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927453", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f1a"], "question": {"text": "For water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mrow><mi>vap</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>41</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>373</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and 1 bar pressure. Assuming that water vapour is an ideal gas that occupies a much larger volume than liquid water, the internal energy change during evaporation of water is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></math>:<br />[ Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mrow><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "34fb8f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927454"}, {"id": "6cc3a1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927455"}, {"id": "94c703", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f80c677dc36a8927456"}, {"id": "5bf240", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_